1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:02,564
What if Delhi's air was
perfectly clean tomorrow?

2
00:00:02,774 --> 00:00:07,150
Every winter, Delhi's air quality often
goes many times above the safe limit.

3
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:09,880
Breathing it is often compared
to smoking cigarettes.

4
00:00:10,045 --> 00:00:11,775
Clean air would change things fast.

5
00:00:11,981 --> 00:00:15,691
Hospitals would see fewer cases
of asthma and breathing problems.

6
00:00:15,786 --> 00:00:17,556
Children could play outside again.

7
00:00:17,597 --> 00:00:19,426
Schools would stay open in November.

8
00:00:19,617 --> 00:00:22,027
Flights and trains wouldn't
be delayed by smog.

9
00:00:22,092 --> 00:00:24,902
And for the first time in months,
people could see the sky,

10
00:00:25,152 --> 00:00:27,602
the stars and the Red Fort from far away.

11
00:00:27,658 --> 00:00:29,028
Clean air should be normal.

12
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:31,503
So what if Delhi's air
became clean tomorrow?

